  "notes": "Source: official University of Dayton sample plan of study for the B.S. in Computer Science, 'for students starting at UD in the 2026-27 academic year' (udayton.edu/academics/programs/computer-science-bs/index.php). The page states: 'This is a sample plan of study for students starting at UD in the 2026-27 academic year. This is a recommended course sequence, but your schedule may vary depending on previously earned college credits, course availability, advisor recommendations and your personal goals and interests.' The page directs readers to the Academic Catalog (catalog.udayton.edu) for official major requirements, prerequisites, and course descriptions; course titles, credit hours, and prerequisites were cross-checked against the catalog's Computer Science course list (catalog.udayton.edu/allcourses/cps/cps.pdf). Degree name verified: the catalog's Computer Science program page lists the program as 'Bachelor of Science, Computer Science' and the department site confirms UD offers a Bachelor of Science in Computer Science. The 2026-27 sample plan uses CPS prefixes for the major core courses; the catalog's course list presents the same core under CSCI prefixes with CPS cross-equivalents (e.g. 'Prerequisite(s): CSCI 151 or CPS 151'), so CPS codes from the plan are retained in the JSON. Prerequisites in the JSON follow the catalog's course descriptions (e.g. CPS 356 requires CPS 250 and CPS 350; CPS 450 requires CPS 341 and CPS 350; CPS 490 requires CPS 420; CPS 491 requires CPS 490). The MTH calculus-chain prerequisites (MTH 169 requires MTH 168; MTH 218 requires MTH 169) are inferred from the official semester ordering, not printed as catalog prerequisite text. Credit discrepancy: the eight semester totals (16+18+16+15+15+15+15+12) sum to 122, while the degree page states the BS requires 'at least 120 credit hours'; total_credits uses the sequence's own published total of 122. The source page carries a footnote '* Choose from PHL 312, 316, 319 or 321' beneath Semester 8 (no explicit requirement named; recorded verbatim as a caveat). ASI 150, HUM 101/102, CAP slots, natural-science slots, and electives are student-choice requirements; their exact courses are chosen by the student, so they are modeled as choice slots. The two 3-credit 'CPS Electives' in Semester 6 are modeled as two separate 3-credit choice slots. Placement/assessment details: none stated in the source; external_prereqs is therefore empty. Transcription method: manual transcription of the official UD sample plan of study on 2026-09-30.",
